<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30276" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">myrtātus</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">murtātus</span></b> , a, um, adj.
		myrtus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>seasoned with myrtle</i> or <i>myrtleberries</i>.—<i>Subst.</i>:
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">murtātum</span></b> ,
				i, n. (sc. farcimen), <i>a kind of pudding</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">murtatum a murtā, quod ea large
					fartum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 5, § 110</span></i>
			 Müll.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>A kind of seasoning</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">form myrtatum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					15, 29, 35, § 118</span></i>
			.</div>
